# Docker does NOT read .gitignore, so everything below would otherwise be
# copied into the image by `COPY . .` — including two things that actively
# break the build.
#
# node_modules: `COPY . .` runs AFTER `npm ci`, so a host node_modules would
# overwrite the one just installed for the image. Prisma ships
# platform-specific query engines, so building on macOS or a different libc
# and copying those in produces a container that installs cleanly and then
# cannot reach the database.
#
# tsconfig.tsbuildinfo: TypeScript reads it, concludes nothing changed, and
# emits nothing — while nest's deleteOutDir has already removed dist/. The
# image then builds "successfully" with an empty dist and the container exits
# with MODULE_NOT_FOUND. (incremental is now off in tsconfig.json, which fixes
# the cause; this keeps a stale file from a previous checkout out regardless.)
node_modules
dist
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

npm-debug.log*
*.log
coverage
test-results

# Editor backups
*.save
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp
